    {
      "id": "source-overview",
      "type": "view",
      "label": "Overview",
      "position": {
        "x": -800,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 460,
      "data": {
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail"
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "ownsContent": true
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Custom Event + Bridge Smoke — Source\n\nExercises two things that have no coverage until now: a custom Event authored by hand (not an intrinsic one like `property.changed`, and not inherited from a class contract), and the direct Method-trigger path for consuming it.\n\n## Widget\n\nA plain Content node. Its only special feature is `data.events`, authored through the Events section on its editor panel (see EventsEditorSection.js): one custom Event, `widget.ready`.\n\n## Local Trigger Demo\n\nA Method wired directly to Widget's `event:widget.ready` output port, into its own `trigger` port — no Event Handler node needed. Open its editor to see the MethodTriggersEditor.js \"TRIGGERS\" section report the live binding, and FixedNode render the wired `event:widget.ready` → `trigger` edge on canvas.\n\n## Export to Receiver\n\nAn export Bridge pointed at `qa/custom-event-bridge-smoke/receiver`, exposing `widget.ready` — ships pre-checked so the pair works end to end as soon as both graphs are open. Uncheck it in the Bridge's Events section to watch the receiver's Handler go inactive.\n\nAutomated coverage for this same scenario: `tests/customEventBridgeSmoke.test.js` in the twilite repo."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "source-declaration",
          "nodeId": "source-overview"
        }
      }
    },
